<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South</p>
<p>American Libertadores Cup first round matches played on</p>
<p>Tuesday.</p>
<p>Group four</p>
<p>In Porto Alegre, Brazil: Gremio (Brazil) 2 Sporting</p>
<p>Cristal (Peru) 0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Paulo Nunes (54), Dauri (82)</p>
<p>Group five</p>
<p>In Montevideo: Nacional (Uruguay) 1 Deportivo Cali</p>
<p>(Colombia) 1 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Nacional -  Juan Ravera (57)</p>
<p>Deportivo Cali - Edson Mafla (37, penalty)</p>
<p>Attendance: 35,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>Group four</p>
<p> Gremio			    6  4  0  2 10  3 12</p>
<p> Cruzeiro (Brazil)	     6  3  0  3  6  5  9</p>
<p> Sporting Cristal		6  2  2  2  4  5  8</p>
<p> Alianza (Peru)		  6  1  2  3  2  9  5</p>
<p>(Gremio, Cruzeiro and Sporting Cristal qualify)</p>
<p>Group five</p>
<p> Millonarios (Colombia)	6  3  1  2 10  8 10</p>
<p> Penarol (Uruguay)	     5  3  0  2  8  7  9</p>
<p> Nacional			  6  2  1  3  6  9  7</p>
<p> Deportivo Cali		  5  1  2  2  6  6  5</p>
<p>Remaining fixture: April 18 - Nacional v Deportivo Cali</p>
<p>(Millonarios and Penarol already qualified)</p>
<p>Note: top three teams in each group go through. Holders</p>
<p>River Plate (Argentina) have a bye to the second round.</p>
</text>
